invariant: INV-16
file: src/rsa_mont64_blocks.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: rsa_mont64_blocks_reduce keeps a where the mask is zero with an
  if, and not with the mask. RSA signing runs this select on values the
  private key decides, so the if is a branch on whether a - m borrowed.
  Every test passes: the words are the same. The pinned clang for arm64
  writes the if as a cbnz on the mask, so rsa_mont64_blocks.c emits 22
  conditional branches where its ceiling is 21.
  inv-16-rsa-blocks-last-subtraction refuses the if too
  (docs/decisions.md 209).

--- old
        o[j] = (o[j] & mask) | (a[j] & ~mask);
    }
    *hidden = 0;
--- new
        if (mask == 0) {
            o[j] = a[j];
        }
    }
    *hidden = 0;
